WEBVTT

00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:23.960
<b>Is It Wrong to Try to Pick Up Girls in a Dungeon? III</b>

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:35.030
Aspiration
Distant Dream

00:01:47.270 --> 00:01:48.300
Food!

00:01:48.630 --> 00:01:50.050
Alcohol!

00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:51.380
And keep it coming!

00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:56.250
For our new kin and our first human guests,
 today, we celebrate!

00:01:56.250 --> 00:01:57.980
Yeah!

00:02:00.310 --> 00:02:02.120
Is this some kind of dream?

00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:04.960
Shall I pinch your cheeks for you?

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:19.220
And then!

00:02:19.220 --> 00:02:21.700
That's when Bell saved me!

00:02:22.190 --> 00:02:23.560
I see.

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:26.150
Bell-san truly is very strange—I mean...

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:28.050
very kind, isn't he?

00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:29.910
"Strange"...

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:31.310
Bell-cchi.

00:02:31.310 --> 00:02:32.500
"Bell-cchi"...

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:36.470
No need to be polite. Eat up! 
We gathered it all around here.

00:02:36.470 --> 00:02:38.730
Apparently, this stuff's 
rare on the surface.

00:02:45.990 --> 00:02:46.910
It's delicious!

00:02:46.910 --> 00:02:47.430
Right?

00:02:50.010 --> 00:02:51.000
Um...

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:53.520
I'm sorry for punching you so hard earlier.

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:55.800
What are you talking about? I did the same.

00:02:57.690 --> 00:02:58.790
If I could ask...

00:02:58.790 --> 00:03:01.410
Is that equipment from adventurers?

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:02.160
Yeah.

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:06.250
Loot from ignorant adventurers 
who came and attacked us.

00:03:06.590 --> 00:03:09.020
When you guys take down a monster,

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:10.860
you take home claws and 
fangs and stuff, right?

00:03:11.240 --> 00:03:14.210
That's... true.

00:03:14.210 --> 00:03:16.810
Human weapons really are amazing.

00:03:16.810 --> 00:03:20.600
They cut way better than any flower or 
plant lying around, and they're hard.

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:23.290
We can't make stuff like this.

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:39.860
Lyd, cease this foolishness.

00:03:42.230 --> 00:03:45.210
In the end, they are humans.

00:03:45.210 --> 00:03:47.070
They are not worthy of trust.

00:03:47.070 --> 00:03:49.050
You still saying that, Gros?

00:03:49.050 --> 00:03:51.880
Bell-cchi and the others have 
been protecting Wiene.

00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:53.600
That's what Fels told us, right?

00:03:53.990 --> 00:03:56.920
It's because you guys said 
you still couldn't accept it

00:03:56.920 --> 00:03:59.140
that we took the rough route back there.

00:04:02.670 --> 00:04:04.150
Sorry about that.

00:04:04.150 --> 00:04:06.860
We've got a lot going on, too.

00:04:06.860 --> 00:04:10.990
When we heard humans were coming 
down here, it set everyone on edge.

00:04:10.990 --> 00:04:12.320
I-It's fine.

00:04:12.630 --> 00:04:15.620
I'm pretty sure they know
that you guys are different

00:04:15.620 --> 00:04:17.760
from other adventurers.

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:23.000
Hey. More importantly, is it true?

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:25.290
The Guild knows about all of you?

00:04:25.290 --> 00:04:26.010
Yeah.

00:04:26.010 --> 00:04:29.170
They take measures to make sure 
we don't get exposed,

00:04:29.170 --> 00:04:30.740
and sometimes they send food or weapons.

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:32.610
They've been helping us a 
lot for a long time now.

00:04:33.430 --> 00:04:37.180
More than the Guild, 
it's the god Ouranos, really.

00:04:37.180 --> 00:04:40.590
Apparently, the people at the Guild 
don't know about us, either.

00:04:40.870 --> 00:04:44.840
Then, the mission we accepted, 
to come down here, was...

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:49.090
Ouranos-sama and his people brought 
it to us, and we agreed to it.

00:04:50.950 --> 00:04:54.950
"To see what the people sheltering one 
of our kin are really like," they said.

00:04:55.730 --> 00:04:58.600
So the patron god of the 
Guild was testing us.

00:04:58.950 --> 00:05:03.240
But, after hearing about Bell-cchi and 
the others, I couldn't help hoping a little.

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:06.690
I thought, maybe, something might change.

00:05:08.660 --> 00:05:11.210
Coexistence between people and monsters?

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:15.010
Do you know what you're saying, Ouranos?

00:05:15.010 --> 00:05:16.280
Of course.

00:05:16.690 --> 00:05:20.590
Conflict between people and monsters has 
been their destiny since ancient times!

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:22.090
Yet you'd still...

00:05:22.090 --> 00:05:25.730
The Xenos do not attack 
simply based on instinct.

00:05:25.730 --> 00:05:27.470
They wish for dialogue with people.

00:05:28.720 --> 00:05:31.080
And it is not those claws and fangs,

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:34.470
but words and reason they 
bring in their appeals.

00:05:34.470 --> 00:05:36.180
That they wish to go to the surface...

00:05:36.180 --> 00:05:39.570
That they wish to know our children...
to know humans.

00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:42.400
The power of reason dwells within the Xenos.

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:44.610
They are attacked even by monsters.

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:46.570
They are alienated and ostracized.

00:05:46.570 --> 00:05:50.230
There is no place for them
even within the labyrinth.

00:05:50.230 --> 00:05:53.870
As they are monsters, it is plain that their 
only choice is to be consigned to oblivion.

00:05:54.190 --> 00:05:56.330
But they have gathered their will,

00:05:56.580 --> 00:05:59.440
and they have the skill to express it,

00:05:59.440 --> 00:06:02.150
just as our children do.

00:06:02.790 --> 00:06:06.540
To watch as they are destroyed, 
unmoved by their lamentations,

00:06:06.540 --> 00:06:08.970
I fear that is no longer something 
which I am able to do.

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:14.090
You're really planning to strive 
toward harmony with monsters?

00:06:14.090 --> 00:06:14.970
Yes.

00:06:15.250 --> 00:06:19.380
But if our aim is co-existence 
with our children,

00:06:19.380 --> 00:06:23.940
then we must inquire into the significance 
of the existence of monsters.

00:06:23.940 --> 00:06:28.930
So the bridge that will make people 
acknowledge value in the existence of monsters

00:06:28.930 --> 00:06:30.770
is Bell-kun and the others?

00:06:30.770 --> 00:06:32.840
That is what I wish to determine.

00:06:34.320 --> 00:06:36.140
I empathize.

00:06:36.140 --> 00:06:41.580
But if our position is exposed, my family 
will lose its place in this town!

00:06:41.990 --> 00:06:43.810
Just like the Xenos.

00:06:44.280 --> 00:06:46.330
I am aware.

00:06:46.330 --> 00:06:48.970
Everything is being done 
at my sole discretion.

00:06:50.130 --> 00:06:52.550
I see. So you were noticed.

00:06:52.960 --> 00:06:54.490
My deepest apologies.

00:06:54.930 --> 00:06:56.430
It seems they sensed I was shadowing them.

00:06:57.560 --> 00:07:01.240
Ikelos's children must have 
some pretty good intuition.

00:07:01.370 --> 00:07:05.150
Dix Perdix, titled "Hazer."

00:07:05.150 --> 00:07:10.000
He is the captain of the familia, and, 
as of ten years ago, was already Level 4.

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:11.200
So what happened to them?

00:07:11.460 --> 00:07:14.150
They scattered and ran. 
I was unable to follow.

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:17.000
They have either returned 
to the surface, or...

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:19.630
Not long from now, 
they'll be plotting something.

00:07:20.210 --> 00:07:22.210
Don't take your eye off the middle floors.

00:07:23.230 --> 00:07:24.580
It really ticks me off!

00:07:24.870 --> 00:07:27.820
If we could have tailed the 
Little Rookie from there,

00:07:27.820 --> 00:07:30.140
we would have found the monsters' nest!

00:07:30.140 --> 00:07:31.830
Didn't have a choice, did we?

00:07:31.830 --> 00:07:34.790
Shaking off the Hermes Familia 
took everything we had.

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:38.710
With that damned god getting in the way...

00:07:40.300 --> 00:07:42.120
But this'll be trouble.

00:07:42.120 --> 00:07:45.010
If people find out we're 
smuggling monsters,

00:07:45.430 --> 00:07:48.360
we'll have to deal with the Guild, as well.

00:07:48.800 --> 00:07:50.400
What are we going to do, Dix?

00:07:50.630 --> 00:07:53.210
The fact they didn't come at us there

00:07:53.210 --> 00:07:55.300
means we've got the upper 
hand in fighting power.

00:07:55.300 --> 00:07:58.960
Besides, you really think we can quit 
doing something that's this much fun?

00:07:59.570 --> 00:08:01.580
The hunt is back on.

00:08:03.870 --> 00:08:09.000
Well, it seems things have once again 
developed in an unexpected direction.

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:10.300
Fels! You came!

00:08:11.280 --> 00:08:12.160
"Fels"?

00:08:15.740 --> 00:08:19.750
Given that Hermes knows about 
Wiene-kun and the Xenos,

00:08:20.140 --> 00:08:22.090
are we the only others who do?

00:08:22.090 --> 00:08:24.980
No. Among the gods, there is one other.

00:08:24.980 --> 00:08:26.300
Ganesha.

00:08:26.300 --> 00:08:27.800
Ganesha?

00:08:27.800 --> 00:08:30.280
I am Ganesha!

00:08:30.280 --> 00:08:32.930
...sha! ...sha! ...sha! ...sha! ...sha!

00:08:33.870 --> 00:08:35.910
Then you can't mean that 
Monsterphilia is...

00:08:35.910 --> 00:08:37.110
That is correct.

00:08:37.420 --> 00:08:41.250
To ease people's revulsion towards monsters,

00:08:41.250 --> 00:08:44.300
Ganesha hosts them at my request.

00:08:44.660 --> 00:08:48.030
To gain his cooperation, 
I explained everything to him.

00:08:49.400 --> 00:08:50.880
You can't be serious.

00:08:50.880 --> 00:08:53.570
Out of everything I've heard today, 
that's the most shocking.

00:08:53.570 --> 00:08:56.330
In spite of appearances, he is 
a god who can keep secrets.

00:08:57.550 --> 00:09:03.110
But to think you've been planning reconciliation
 between monsters and people for that long.

00:09:04.410 --> 00:09:06.930
First, I shall say I am pleased to meet you.

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:09.270
I am Fels.

00:09:09.270 --> 00:09:13.750
Conveying communications between Ouranos and 
Lyd and the Xenos is the bulk of my duties.

00:09:15.040 --> 00:09:20.210
For the past seven days, I have watched 
over you and the dragon maiden.

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:21.730
You have...

00:09:22.020 --> 00:09:24.450
Fels has eyes all over the place.

00:09:24.450 --> 00:09:27.720
With this one, they can 
contact us at any time.

00:09:28.140 --> 00:09:31.920
Fels-sama, are you a monster, too?

00:09:32.260 --> 00:09:34.710
Nope, Fels is a human.

00:09:34.710 --> 00:09:37.480
To be precise, a former human.

00:09:37.480 --> 00:09:38.210
What?

00:09:38.990 --> 00:09:41.050
I shall show you, as well.

00:09:43.300 --> 00:09:44.650
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!

00:09:44.650 --> 00:09:46.680
A monster?! A spartoi?

00:09:47.110 --> 00:09:50.220
I did tell you. A former human.

00:09:50.220 --> 00:09:52.470
Wh-What does that mean?

00:09:52.770 --> 00:09:55.930
Fels is a sage! A super-amazing mage!

00:09:56.160 --> 00:09:57.410
Sage? You mean...

00:09:57.410 --> 00:09:59.990
In that one well-known, great nation 
of sages... The philosopher's stone...

00:09:59.990 --> 00:10:03.100
Only one person managed to successfully 
create it and gain eternal life!

00:10:03.100 --> 00:10:04.280
That sage?

00:10:04.280 --> 00:10:07.610
Huh? Yeah... They might be that sage.

00:10:08.980 --> 00:10:10.250
That is correct.

00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:13.830
I am the remaining ruins of one 
who was once called a sage.

00:10:14.260 --> 00:10:18.830
In my pursuit of infinite wisdom, 
I became obsessed with eternal life.

00:10:19.130 --> 00:10:22.100
I devised a secret formula to 
become undying and regenerative,

00:10:22.300 --> 00:10:24.500
and I became a living ghost.

00:10:25.010 --> 00:10:28.640
Now, I am known as Fels the Fool.

00:10:30.220 --> 00:10:32.130
At Ouranos's side,

00:10:32.130 --> 00:10:35.460
I observe the shifting of the ages.

00:10:39.060 --> 00:10:44.200
I first made contact with Lyd and 
the others over 15 years ago.

00:10:44.770 --> 00:10:50.210
We called them "Xenos," and created 
a community by the same name.

00:10:50.760 --> 00:10:54.300
An organization to shelter their kin,
 born of the Dungeon,

00:10:54.300 --> 00:10:56.100
and allow them to live together.

00:10:56.890 --> 00:11:00.370
Since then, so that other 
monsters don't find us,

00:11:00.370 --> 00:11:05.670
we move through the labyrinth, 
living together, looking for new kin.

00:11:05.930 --> 00:11:08.060
Living together...

00:11:08.060 --> 00:11:11.130
Doesn't this room give birth to monsters?

00:11:11.380 --> 00:11:14.530
Hey! That's a good point you've 
noticed there, Lili-cchi!

00:11:14.530 --> 00:11:15.890
"Lili-cchi"...

00:11:16.390 --> 00:11:20.130
This is unexplored territory that 
adventurers haven't found yet.

00:11:20.130 --> 00:11:22.940
A place where monsters 
aren't born. A safe point.

00:11:23.420 --> 00:11:25.950
We call it a hidden village.

00:11:26.320 --> 00:11:29.640
The Dungeon has several spaces like this.

00:11:29.640 --> 00:11:30.910
Is that right?

00:11:33.710 --> 00:11:35.950
There are approximately forty Xenos here.

00:11:36.270 --> 00:11:40.460
Among them, Lyd, Rei, and Gros 
have been members the longest.

00:11:42.240 --> 00:11:44.640
Then... are you the leader?

00:11:44.960 --> 00:11:48.700
Yeah. And I'm also the strongest, too.

00:11:48.700 --> 00:11:50.700
At least, that's what I'd like to say.

00:11:50.700 --> 00:11:54.490
But recently, a newcomer who 
joined us has passed me up.

00:11:54.820 --> 00:11:56.030
Really?

00:11:56.030 --> 00:11:57.780
Y-Yeah...

00:11:57.780 --> 00:12:01.200
Even now, the newcomer's gone down 
to the deeper levels alone to train.

00:12:01.200 --> 00:12:05.410
Probably planning to get 
even stronger, that one!

00:12:06.880 --> 00:12:12.450
But, Fels-sama, why do you and 
the others support the Xenos?

00:12:12.450 --> 00:12:15.810
In their position, there is 
no need to give them aid.

00:12:16.360 --> 00:12:20.190
Though it is dangerous, they are more than 
capable of living here in the Dungeon.

00:12:20.730 --> 00:12:25.710
Fels-sama, what is it that the Xenos 
seek through their connection to you?

00:12:30.240 --> 00:12:32.320
To emerge on the surface.

00:12:32.950 --> 00:12:35.150
That is our wish.

00:12:38.140 --> 00:12:39.830
I have this dream...

00:12:39.830 --> 00:12:43.640
A dream where this crimson light 
sinks behind giant rocks.

00:12:44.380 --> 00:12:49.150
A sky that doesn't exist here 
is dyed red enough to cry red.

00:12:49.150 --> 00:12:51.020
Is that a sunset?

00:12:51.020 --> 00:12:52.750
Have you ever been to the surface?

00:12:53.570 --> 00:12:54.300
No.

00:12:54.820 --> 00:12:56.090
Not even once.

00:12:56.500 --> 00:12:58.680
That's why I think maybe...

00:12:59.290 --> 00:13:03.850
The last time I lived, I might have 
been somewhere I could see the sky.

00:13:03.850 --> 00:13:05.870
The "last time you lived"?

00:13:07.860 --> 00:13:08.720
Bell-cchi...

00:13:09.020 --> 00:13:11.770
Wiene learned how to speak 
really quickly, right?

00:13:11.770 --> 00:13:13.440
Huh? Yes.

00:13:14.360 --> 00:13:18.390
Here, we have both those who 
can speak and those who can't.

00:13:18.670 --> 00:13:23.060
The ones who can speak, for some reason,
 they learn how really fast.

00:13:23.060 --> 00:13:27.780
It's just like they're remembering 
that they've spoken before.

00:13:29.170 --> 00:13:31.590
My body grows cold.

00:13:32.130 --> 00:13:35.720
My chest is empty, as though 
there was a hole in it.

00:13:35.720 --> 00:13:38.630
I see those people so clearly...

00:13:39.830 --> 00:13:41.890
An intense, severe longing...

00:13:42.380 --> 00:13:45.690
The feelings hidden in 
their hearts are varied.

00:13:45.690 --> 00:13:51.340
But an intense aspiration towards humanity, 
or the surface, is the sole commonality.

00:13:51.720 --> 00:13:55.090
I want to see that sunset one more time.

00:13:55.340 --> 00:13:58.750
I want to try spreading my 
wings in a world of light.

00:13:59.200 --> 00:14:02.290
In place of these wings, 
which can embrace no one...

00:14:02.850 --> 00:14:05.110
I want to be embraced by someone I love.

00:14:05.590 --> 00:14:06.970
We know.

00:14:07.360 --> 00:14:09.480
We're outcasts, meant to live in the shade.

00:14:09.840 --> 00:14:13.490
We're neither one thing nor the other, 
hated by both people and monsters.

00:14:13.980 --> 00:14:15.220
Even this place...

00:14:15.220 --> 00:14:20.250
We think maybe our mom 
might've prepared it for us.

00:14:20.540 --> 00:14:21.640
"Mom"?

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:24.460
The Dungeon which gave birth to us.

00:14:24.990 --> 00:14:28.790
We were attacked by our own kind,
 our lives targeted...

00:14:29.220 --> 00:14:34.400
But at the same time, our existence 
is permitted by our mother, the labyrinth.

00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:36.880
That is what we believe.

00:14:37.220 --> 00:14:38.620
That's why, see?

00:14:38.620 --> 00:14:41.300
Why we were so happy to meet 
you and the others, Bell-cchi!

00:14:41.670 --> 00:14:44.870
It's not about wanting you 
to help us or anything.

00:14:44.870 --> 00:14:49.150
It's just the fact that people 
who can accept us exist.

00:14:50.740 --> 00:14:53.130
Bell-cchi, I'm glad 
I met you and the others!

00:14:54.520 --> 00:14:58.370
Ouranos, allow me to ask one final question.

00:14:58.590 --> 00:14:59.640
What is it?

00:14:59.640 --> 00:15:02.300
What in the world is
happening in the Dungeon?

00:15:02.300 --> 00:15:05.670
Do you know why the Xenos are being born?

00:15:08.400 --> 00:15:11.100
What do you think happens 
to monsters after they die?

00:15:11.100 --> 00:15:12.290
What are you talking about?

00:15:12.840 --> 00:15:15.750
Our children's spirits return to Heaven,

00:15:15.750 --> 00:15:18.560
and they are once again given 
life in this Lower World.

00:15:18.560 --> 00:15:22.160
Then where do you think 
monsters' spirits go?

00:15:22.600 --> 00:15:23.780
You can't mean...

00:15:23.780 --> 00:15:27.590
The spirits of monsters return 
to their mother, the labyrinth.

00:15:27.590 --> 00:15:32.850
Then, in a different form, they are 
born in the depths of the labyrinth.

00:15:33.160 --> 00:15:35.560
The monsters have a cycle 
of death and rebirth!

00:15:36.010 --> 00:15:37.950
This is no more than supposition.

00:15:38.220 --> 00:15:40.700
But I am confident in my belief.

00:15:40.700 --> 00:15:44.520
Over thousands of years, 
through countless rebirths,

00:15:44.520 --> 00:15:46.820
their wishes and regrets have layered,
 one on another,

00:15:46.820 --> 00:15:49.600
and now try to change the 
nature of their souls.

00:15:50.120 --> 00:15:51.180
But why?

00:15:51.500 --> 00:15:55.870
It is either the strength of 
the monsters' yearning, or...

00:15:55.870 --> 00:15:57.500
the will of the Dungeon.

00:15:59.410 --> 00:16:01.980
Thank you for today, truly.

00:16:01.980 --> 00:16:03.130
I am glad to have met you.

00:16:03.390 --> 00:16:05.290
W-We should be thanking you.

00:16:05.290 --> 00:16:07.100
Bell-cchi, do you know what this is?

00:16:07.430 --> 00:16:10.190
Huh? A monster's magic stone?

00:16:13.020 --> 00:16:17.040
We get attacked by other monsters 
without a chance to talk.

00:16:17.040 --> 00:16:19.980
And we, too, kill monsters to survive.

00:16:23.180 --> 00:16:26.760
We eat magic stones this way and 
use them to strengthen ourselves.

00:16:27.520 --> 00:16:30.630
So, please, don't hesitate 
about killing monsters.

00:16:30.630 --> 00:16:33.500
Don't waver out of consideration for us.

00:16:33.980 --> 00:16:36.770
If you hesitate, Bell-cchi, you will die.

00:16:40.470 --> 00:16:42.460
Make sure you don't die, okay?

00:16:42.980 --> 00:16:44.110
I want to see you again.

00:16:55.010 --> 00:16:57.210
Bell! That was fun, wasn't it?

00:16:57.570 --> 00:16:59.250
Let's go home together!

00:16:59.480 --> 00:17:01.400
You're with us, Wiene.

00:17:01.400 --> 00:17:03.760
No! Put me down!

00:17:03.760 --> 00:17:06.580
I can't! You're with us!

00:17:06.580 --> 00:17:08.880
No! I want to be with Bell!

00:17:08.880 --> 00:17:12.210
If you're with them, you're going
to make Bell-cchi and the others cry!

00:17:09.840 --> 00:17:10.920
Let go!

00:17:12.420 --> 00:17:13.150
What?

00:17:14.360 --> 00:17:16.920
They treated you terribly on 
the surface, didn't they?

00:17:16.920 --> 00:17:20.960
Next time, all of that will be turned 
toward Bell-san and the others.

00:17:22.000 --> 00:17:25.260
We can't live on the surface yet.

00:17:25.550 --> 00:17:28.390
But here, no one will hurt you.

00:17:28.870 --> 00:17:30.730
You're going to live here with us.

00:17:34.230 --> 00:17:35.120
Bell...

00:17:35.740 --> 00:17:36.970
I...

00:17:38.730 --> 00:17:40.770
See you around, Bell-cchi.

00:17:41.580 --> 00:17:42.590
Bell!

00:17:43.130 --> 00:17:44.370
Bell!

00:17:44.780 --> 00:17:47.150
Bell!

00:17:49.180 --> 00:17:50.450
We'll see each other!

00:17:50.870 --> 00:17:52.830
We'll see each other again!

00:17:53.180 --> 00:17:55.950
Bell!

00:18:10.200 --> 00:18:11.260
We're back.

00:18:11.260 --> 00:18:13.640
Welcome back, Bell-kun, everyone.

00:18:15.240 --> 00:18:16.340
Goddess...

00:18:17.290 --> 00:18:19.270
What is the Dungeon?

00:18:21.030 --> 00:18:23.030
The Dungeon is the Dungeon.

00:18:27.970 --> 00:18:30.920
It's just about time to set out, Wiene.

00:18:31.390 --> 00:18:31.760
Okay.

00:18:33.280 --> 00:18:34.880
You're late, Wiene.

00:18:35.540 --> 00:18:39.230
We may not make it by the time we're meant 
to meet up with the advance party.

00:18:39.970 --> 00:18:41.400
I'm sorry.

00:18:45.740 --> 00:18:47.390
Thank you, Foh.

00:18:48.810 --> 00:18:50.440
Stop dawdling!

00:18:50.440 --> 00:18:52.850
While we're moving, anything could happen.

00:18:52.850 --> 00:18:55.990
Until we reach the new village, 
absolutely do not let your guard down!

00:18:55.990 --> 00:18:56.980
Understood!

00:19:01.100 --> 00:19:03.380
Why are we moving villages?

00:19:03.380 --> 00:19:05.600
Did someone find us?

00:19:05.600 --> 00:19:09.460
Out of caution against the unlikely 
event of a raid, we change positions.

00:19:10.210 --> 00:19:15.160
And if we stay in the same spot for 
too long, we run out of things to eat.

00:19:15.160 --> 00:19:16.640
I see...

00:19:18.270 --> 00:19:20.960
Mikoto's food was really yummy.

00:19:20.960 --> 00:19:22.650
Don't worry!

00:19:22.650 --> 00:19:27.040
Those people from the surface, 
Bell-san and the others, you'll see them again.

00:19:27.530 --> 00:19:28.150
Yes.

00:19:28.150 --> 00:19:30.060
Are you still saying those things?

00:19:30.060 --> 00:19:31.950
Forget those humans.

00:19:32.400 --> 00:19:35.250
Wiene, they will only cause you harm.

00:19:36.900 --> 00:19:39.880
Ranieh, do you hate Bell and the others?

00:19:39.880 --> 00:19:42.950
Bell and Haruhime and the 
Goddess were all kind to me!

00:19:42.950 --> 00:19:46.710
That was simply a whim of theirs.
 You are too ignorant.

00:19:47.060 --> 00:19:50.180
You know nothing of their cruelty or cunning.

00:19:53.150 --> 00:19:54.220
Wiene?

00:19:54.790 --> 00:19:56.520
I can hear it...

00:19:56.520 --> 00:20:00.620
Someone crying... saying "help me!"

00:20:00.620 --> 00:20:01.970
The voice of our kin?

00:20:01.970 --> 00:20:03.000
Yes.

00:20:03.180 --> 00:20:05.650
So much suffering...

00:20:05.650 --> 00:20:08.150
If we don't help soon...

00:20:08.910 --> 00:20:10.750
What do we do, Ranieh?

00:20:10.750 --> 00:20:12.800
In these circumstances, 
every moment must be fought for.

00:20:13.200 --> 00:20:14.220
We go!

00:20:21.560 --> 00:20:24.330
We're very close.

00:20:24.330 --> 00:20:26.980
Yes. I can hear it, too.

00:20:26.980 --> 00:20:28.390
Gros, can you hear me?

00:20:28.390 --> 00:20:30.520
We are going to rescue new kin.

00:20:30.520 --> 00:20:32.490
Please, wait for us at the meeting point.

00:20:32.490 --> 00:20:33.900
<i>Wait, Ranieh!</i>

00:20:33.900 --> 00:20:35.560
<i>It's too dangerous with just your group!</i>

00:20:35.560 --> 00:20:37.080
<i>We'll come support you!</i>

00:20:37.950 --> 00:20:39.700
After hearing this voice...

00:20:40.010 --> 00:20:41.420
We can't wait!

00:20:41.420 --> 00:20:44.090
<i>Ranieh! Stop! It could be a trap—</i>

00:20:58.170 --> 00:21:01.410
Run...

00:21:03.640 --> 00:21:05.760
So you really can cry...

00:21:05.760 --> 00:21:07.890
you monsters.

00:21:13.220 --> 00:21:14.120
Adventurers?

00:21:14.120 --> 00:21:15.510
An ambush?

00:21:16.620 --> 00:21:18.880
It all went exactly as planned.

00:21:19.290 --> 00:21:21.880
To lure in a vouivre, 
with her excellent hearing,

00:21:21.880 --> 00:21:25.330
a screaming siren is the perfect choice.

00:21:28.070 --> 00:21:29.290
You evil, scheming...

00:21:43.000 --> 00:21:43.610
Orde!

00:21:44.050 --> 00:21:45.580
Gran, you moron.

00:21:45.580 --> 00:21:48.560
What if there was a monster 
we could have sold in there?

00:21:48.940 --> 00:21:51.340
Sorry, Dix. Couldn't help myself.

00:21:52.420 --> 00:21:54.840
Not as many as I thought there'd be.

00:21:55.150 --> 00:21:57.340
Kills my motivation.

00:21:57.610 --> 00:21:59.840
Guess I won't need to use this, will I?

00:22:01.990 --> 00:22:03.330
All right.

00:22:03.330 --> 00:22:04.040
Let's hunt.

00:23:36.020 --> 00:23:41.020
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:36.020 --> 00:23:41.020
<b>Ikelos Familia
King of Atrocity</b>

00:23:37.510 --> 00:23:40.200
Next time, "Ikelos Familia."
